# TyrannoPrimeval (22215), every draw 0, told to report (event 11049, i_quest2 1) with another TyrannoPrimeval 3000 away, both far from the character: once
# its report timer (600 s) ran, it broadcasts the script event 11051 (arguments 0 and the range 8000) to the NPCs around
# it; dying while reporting it broadcasts 11044 (0, 0 and the range 5000). The reference run records what the other
# one hears. The monsters list no skill, so the lethal hit asks for no cast.
trace internal/gameserver/script/testdata/oracle/scenarios/tyranno_primeval_broadcasts.golden
character Hunter 20
random always 0
script script.ai.individual.DefaultNpc
script script.ai.individual.Monster.MonsterAI
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.WarriorBase
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.Warrior
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.TyrannoPrimeval.TyrannoPrimeval
npc rex 22215 Monster 4000 0 0
npc listener 22215 Monster 7000 0 0

event rex 11049 0 0
advance 600s
kill rex
  S NpcSay obj=rex type=1 npc=1022215 text="Our master now comes to claim our vengeance. Soon you will all be nothing more than dirt..."
